From: DeskPort maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] stream-source: keep the stream alive while emitting closed

PipeWire core loss emits the source's closed signal. Its handler stops the
stream and can release the session's last stream reference. Signal emission
keeps the source alive until it returns, but the source only borrows its stream.
The resulting source disposal dereferences the freed stream while looking up
the backend/monitor manager (observed in meta_stream_source_virtual_dispose).

Retain the stream across signal emission so source disposal still has a valid
backend. This patch targets Mutter 51; it is a compositor fix, not a patch to
the DeskPort executable or an instruction to replace a running desktop.

--- a/src/backends/meta-stream-source.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-stream-source.c
@@ -2942,7 +2942,12 @@ pipewire_loop_source_dispatch (GSource     *base_source,
     g_warning ("pipewire_loop_iterate failed: %s", spa_strerror (result));
 
   if (priv->emit_closed_after_dispatch)
-    g_signal_emit (source, signals[CLOSED], 0);
+    {
+      /* The closed handlers may release the stream before signal emission
+       * releases its temporary source reference. Source disposal needs it. */
+      g_autoptr (MetaStream) stream = g_object_ref (priv->stream);
+      g_signal_emit (source, signals[CLOSED], 0);
+    }
 
   return G_SOURCE_CONTINUE;
 }
